desc:ReaProof Gain BROKEN (does not compile)
// Deliberately-broken variant for the JSFX battery: db2gain() is DEFINED in
// @gfx but CALLED from @slider. JSFX compiles @gfx after the other sections,
// so the reference is undefined and the WHOLE file fails to compile — yet
// REAPER still inserts it, still lists the declared sliders as live params,
// and passes audio through bit-exact (catalog item 1, mequaz, forum t=310135
// post #5; failure mode live-verified on REAPER 7.75). Only the FX window
// carries the compiler error text — which is exactly what the battery reads.

slider1:0<-24,24,0.01>Gain (dB)

in_pin:left input
in_pin:right input
out_pin:left output
out_pin:right output

@init
gain = 1;

@slider
gain = db2gain(slider1);

@sample
spl0 *= gain;
spl1 *= gain;

@gfx 100 60
function db2gain(db) ( 10^(db/20) );
gfx_x = 4; gfx_y = 4;
gfx_printf("%.2f dB", slider1);
